@page "/foundation"

<PageTitle>OVP-000 · OneVision.UI</PageTitle>

<div class="ov-index-heading">
    <div>
        <div class="ov-home-kicker">@OneVision.UI.Foundation.OneVisionApplicationFoundation.Reference · Contract v@OneVision.UI.Foundation.OneVisionApplicationFoundation.ContractVersion</div>
        <h1 class="ov-gallery-page-title">OneVision Application Foundation</h1>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="ov-gallery-page-intro">
            The root governed UI contract adopted by every OneVision application before screen-by-screen component or pattern migration.
        </MudText>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="ov-home-section">
    <MudPaper Class="ov-library-card" Elevation="0">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">First adoption state</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-4">
            Adopt OVP-000 at the application composition root first, including the governed OVP-001 application shell. This deliberately exposes legacy global overrides so they can be resolved rather than silently preserved as a second design system.
        </MudText>
        <pre class="ov-code">services.AddOneVisionUI();

&lt;link rel="stylesheet"
      href="_content/OneVision.UI/onevision.css" /&gt;</pre>
    </MudPaper>
</section>

<section class="ov-home-section">
    <div class="ov-home-two-column">
        <MudPaper Class="ov-library-card" Elevation="0">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Foundation owns</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Typography, design tokens, density, shared control defaults, common states, provider expectations, accessibility, application shell and reusable page-layout structure.</MudText>
        </MudPaper>
        <MudPaper Class="ov-library-card" Elevation="0">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Applications own</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Domain data, permissions, business rules and app-specific composition. Existing OVC/OVP standards are used where available; genuine reusable gaps belong back in OneVision.UI.</MudText>
        </MudPaper>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="ov-home-section">
    <MudPaper Class="ov-home-example" Elevation="0">
        <div>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Governed shell & layouts</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">OVP-001 and OVP-010–013 provide the standard application frame and page structures beneath this foundation.</MudText>
        </div>
        <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" Href="layouts">View shell & layouts</MudButton>
    </MudPaper>
</section>

<section class="ov-home-section">
    <MudPaper Class="ov-home-example" Elevation="0">
        <div>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Versioned contract</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">The library exposes a machine-readable contract identity so apps can prove the baseline they implement.</MudText>
        </div>
        <pre class="ov-code">Reference: @OneVision.UI.Foundation.OneVisionApplicationFoundation.Reference
Version:   @OneVision.UI.Foundation.OneVisionApplicationFoundation.ContractVersion</pre>
    </MudPaper>
</section>

<section class="ov-home-section">
    <MudPaper Class="ov-library-card" Elevation="0">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Change rule</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            Every foundation-affecting library change gets a contract-impact assessment. The OVP-000 version advances only when externally observable foundation rules change, and the implementation, contract documentation and gallery must be updated together.
        </MudText>
    </MudPaper>
</section>
